  "description": "The HITL proposal-kind vocabulary (ADR-0015, schema plan 5). Seeded into proposal_kinds at boot (constitution rule 7b: extensible domain vocabulary = seeded lookup + FK, never a CHECK). id is the durable vocabulary value referenced by proposals.kind_id; card_variant is the ADR-0015 wire card key the chat UI registers a handler under; schema_ref names the pydantic model that validates final_payload before any write (trust boundary); resolver names the server-side apply path (client_committed = the UI already wrote through the canonical REST endpoint, record_only = nothing is written). Adding a kind is an entry here + a row, never a migration.",
